&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring our first dedicated data governance team member to help build and scale our Data &amp;amp; System Governance processes and tools. As the Accounting Enablement Manager, you’ll own the day-to-day administration, support, and optimization of ERP-related master data objects. While operational support is a core responsibility, you’ll also contribute to automation initiatives, system enhancements, and cross-functional projects that improve business processes and bring efficiency. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys solving complex problems, improving processes, and growing into ownership of increasingly strategic initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has a strong foundation in accounting processes, hands-on experience with data analysis, strong project management skills, and the ability to work across departments to solve problems in a fast-paced environment with conflicting priorities. In this position you will act as end-to-end owner of the master data lifecycle while driving data governance best practices and owning data dictionaries for key finance objects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and publish data governance policies, standards, procedures, and guidelines for master data domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the business glossary and data dictionary for key finance master data objects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process improvement opportunities to streamline master data requests, approvals, and maintenance of workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor compliance with governance policies and escalate issues as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform data profiling, quality assessment, and KPI reporting on governance metrics, and support root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate governance council or data stewardship councils with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5+ years of data analysis experience, with hands-on experience in master data management, data governance, or data analysis within a Finance organization at a publicly listed company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and enforcing data standards, policies, and procedures across cross-functional teams in a SOX-compliant environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and time-management skills, and a builder mindset with a focus on delivering scalable and reliable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and problem-solving skills, and the ability to operate independently in a fast-paced environment with agility in the face of ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit? We believe in investing in our people and value candidates who bring diverse experiences—even if you don’t meet every requirement. Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve supported system implementations, migrations, and re-architecture of an ERP system (e.g. NetSuite, S/4 HANA, Oracle).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring project management experience and can prioritize and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve integrated finance systems and used data querying tools, and you’re familiar with data catalog and metadata management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization’s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $115,000 to $153,000. The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance - 100% paid for by CoreWeave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary supplemental life insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and long-term disability insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to Participate in Employee Stock Purchase Program (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellness Benefits through Spring Health&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-Forming support provided by Carrot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental Leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, full-service childcare support with Kinside&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with a generous employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunch each day in our office and data center locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A casual work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
