&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Data Center Operations team serves as the backbone of our infrastructure, ensuring the seamless performance of our global hyperscale environment. Operating in a high-stakes, 24/7 setting, this team is responsible for safeguarding the availability, stability, and reliability of mission-critical systems that power our most essential services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Command Center Technician, you will serve as the front-line mission control for our global data center fleet. Where a site technician walks the floor, you walk the fleet — conducting structured remote rounds across every site we operate, using BMS, EPMS, DCIM, and every other telemetry source available to us. In a 24/7 operations environment, you will be responsible for real-time monitoring, coordination, and incident response across critical electrical, mechanical, and environmental systems. Acting as the central point of visibility, you will identify anomalies, coordinate cross-functional response efforts, and drive rapid resolution to ensure maximum uptime, operational continuity, and safety across our infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote monitoring role. You will not be turning wrenches — you will be the reason the person turning the wrench knows where to go.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct scheduled remote rounds each shift, reviewing and recording the health of electrical, mechanical, and fire/life safety systems across the fleet to ensure 24/7 reliability and availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide continuous monitoring of global data center infrastructure using Building Management Systems (BMS), Electrical Power Management Systems (EPMS), DCIM, and all other available telemetry and observability platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor critical assets including UPS systems, standby generators and fuel systems, switchgear, PDUs, battery plant, chillers, CRAH/CRAC units, cooling towers, pumps, air handlers, and fire suppression systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Baseline normal operating conditions and identify deviations, drift, and early-warning signatures in telemetry before they escalate into events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the first responder for infrastructure alarms, triaging incidents and initiating response actions per SOPs, MOPs, and EOPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate incidents promptly to on-site operations, engineering teams, and leadership based on defined escalation matrices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate incident response activities across multiple teams and multiple sites to minimize risk to production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dispatch and remotely support on-site technicians, vendors, and contractors during events and planned maintenance, confirming work is performed in accordance with established practices and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support root cause analysis (RCA) efforts by providing detailed timelines, logs, alarm histories, and incident documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a central communication hub, providing clear and accurate status updates during incidents and maintenance events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform technical writing in support of the change management program, including event narratives, procedure feedback, and shift documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce adherence to change management processes and safety requirements within mission-critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage daily work requests and alarm queues to resolution within defined internal service levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain detailed event logs and participate in structured shift handovers to ensure operational continuity across crews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make timely, high-quality decisions in high-pressure situations while maintaining a strong focus on safety, uptime, and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Schedule:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Command Center operates 24/7/365. This is a permanent night shift position on a 12.5-hour schedule. It does not rotate to days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shift: 12.5 hours, nights, with the shift scheduled to include a 30-minute handover overlap at each end of the night.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rotation: A fixed two-week repeating pattern (2-2-3) with every other weekend off. Depending on crew assignment, you will work either:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sunday, Wednesday, Thursday in week one; Monday, Tuesday, Friday, Saturday in week two — or&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monday, Tuesday, Friday, Saturday in week one; Sunday, Wednesday, Thursday in week two.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle: Three scheduled shifts in one week and four in the next, repeating. You will never work more than four shifts in a single week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Days off: Every other weekend off, plus a four-day break built into each two-week cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holidays: The Command Center is staffed on holidays. Holiday coverage is part of the rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handover: Every shift begins and ends with a structured handover to the oncoming and outgoing crew. Punctuality is a safety requirement, not a preference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-site presence: This role is performed from the Command Center and requires on-site presence for the duration of each shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a salaried, exempt position.&lt;/p&gt;
