&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years of progressive accounting experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including senior leadership roles, with broad ownership of technical, operational, cost, or reporting accounting in a high-value, asset-heavy, capital-intensive, or logistics-intensive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong command of U.S. GAAP and internal controls:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep technical background in U.S. GAAP as applied to inventory valuation, cost accounting, fixed assets/PP&amp;amp;E, CIP, and procure-to-pay, with proven experience designing and operating SOX-compliant (or equivalent) internal control frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems &amp;amp; ERP transformation leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience leading or owning the accounting design for an ERP implementation, migration, or major upgrade (NetSuite, SAP, Oracle, Dynamics, or comparable).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven team builder &amp;amp; player-coach:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to lead, coach, and scale accounting teams in high-growth, fast-paced environments — equally comfortable setting long-term strategy and diving into technical execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional leadership &amp;amp; stakeholder management:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong executive presence and communication skills, with a track record of partnering cross-functionally with Operations, Supply Chain, Procurement, FP&amp;amp;A, and IT to achieve measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
