&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience, including 1+ year directly managing engineers on platform, infrastructure, or internal developer teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building or operating CI, build or artifact platforms at scale - CI pipelines, release automation, build systems, or artifact management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of SDLC practices, code review workflows, and branching/release strategies (e.g., trunk-based development).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge or hands-on experience with Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and mentoring engineers, with a track record of supporting individual growth and team execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable defining, tracking and continuously improving business metrics (reliability, velocity, quality) for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion of using automation and AI to reduce toil and improve velocity and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of cloud platforms, containerization, and modern CI / build practices such as GitHub Actions, JFrog Artifactory, Bazel, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools such as Terraform, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator, able to represent your team&#39;s work and technical tradeoffs to both engineers and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
