&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Engineering organization is responsible for executing and delivering CoreWeave’s products, platforms, processes, and tools. As a security technical program leader focused on Operational Technology (OT) Security and Network Security, you will work across cross-functional teams — including security engineering, physical security, data center operations, threat intelligence, TPRM, legal, and network engineering — to build authoritative visibility, close architectural gaps, and drive accountability across owned data centers and third-party colocation providers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are passionate about identity, access, and cloud security, thrive in complex technical environments, and excel at orchestrating large-scale programs, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up CoreWeave&#39;s OT Security program from the ground up — spanning networking, architecture, asset management, and vulnerability management — across data centers CoreWeave owns and operates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Data Center Operations team to build and maintain an authoritative OT asset inventory across power infrastructure, cooling/HVAC, building management systems (BMS), environmental sensors, and physical security systems (e.g., Genetec, badge access, biometrics, cameras), including ownership and criticality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and operationalize an OT vulnerability management lifecycle — discovery, prioritization, remediation SLAs, and exception handling — suited to systems that can&#39;t be patched like standard IT assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive compliance, assurance, and accountability for OT security across third-party colocation providers, including defining the standards CoreWeave expects, the evidence required to demonstrate them, and escalation paths when providers fall short&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive CoreWeave&#39;s Network Security program, maintaining authoritative visibility into production network devices, configurations, ownership, and access rules, with a defined process for tracking and resolving material gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the security standards and controls for network device administration and access policy, ensuring requirements are consistently enforced, verified, and reviewed through a formal exception process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the Network Security program to scale across new global sites and deployment models as CoreWeave expands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner day-to-day with a primary Security Engineering Manager and Technical Lead across Network Security and OT Security to translate technical priorities into sequenced, resourced program plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As programs are defined and stood up, clearly define program strategy, scope, milestones, and success metrics while managing risks and dependencies across both workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact for cross-functional stakeholders, providing regular status updates, addressing risks, and ensuring accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailor communications to a diverse audience — from data center operations and network engineers to the CISO organization and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of hands-on Technical Program Management experience, with a strong focus on security, data center infrastructure, or network engineering programs, including experience standing up a program from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in Information Security, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent job experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of OT/ICS environments and their common systems (power distribution, UPS/generators, cooling/HVAC, BMS, environmental monitoring) or of physical security systems (access control, biometrics, video management/Genetec-class platforms)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of network security fundamentals — segmentation, access control lists, administrative access hardening, and network device configuration management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to convert ambiguous, cross-functional problems into a scoped program with clear ownership, milestones, and measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving accountability with third parties (vendors, colocation providers, OEMs) on security requirements, including defining evidence standards and escalation paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in program management tools and methodologies (e.g., Jira, hands-on dashboard development), with a focus on delivering measurable results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, interpersonal, and influencing skills, with a proven ability to build relationships across technical and non-technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead cross-functional teams to prioritize, manage tradeoffs, identify gaps and risks, drive accountability, and operate autonomously across multiple teams and organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience securing OT/ICS environments in a data center, critical infrastructure, energy, manufacturing, or industrial setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with OT-specific frameworks and standards (e.g., NIST SP 800-82, IEC 62443, Purdue Model)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running network device inventory, hardening, or default-deny control-plane initiatives at scale (multi-site or multi-region)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with colocation or multi-tenant data center models, including provider governance and audit/assurance processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a fast-moving environment and flexible working with a variety of leadership styles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp; We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. The organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
