&lt;li&gt;B.S. or B.A. degree in Construction, Architecture, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 7 years of construction project management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 3 years of direct experience managing data center construction projects with a strong emphasis on MEP (Mechanical, Electrical, Plumbing) systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing projects with a contract value of $100M+.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of data center infrastructure, including power distribution, cooling systems, and redundancy protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of construction components, processes, methodologies, and cost estimation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with web-based project management software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A valid driver&#39;s license with no significant MVA points/violations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting on-site progress inspections and verifying contractor work against drawings, specifications, and the master schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP (Project Management Professional) Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LEED AP (Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design Accredited Professional) Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with electrical and low-voltage equipment coordination, commissioning, or quality assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
