&lt;li&gt;Help define the global mobility strategy, service model, policies, escalation paths, and decision rights across immigration, relocation, and cross-border work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a consistent framework for assessing business need, legal feasibility, employee experience, cost, risk, and timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build operating rhythms for case reviews, vendor governance, stakeholder updates, audits, and leadership reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise People leadership on program priorities, capacity, risk tolerance, and investments required to support international growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Immigration and work authorization&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee immigration case intake, triage, approvals, filings, document collection, status tracking, and employee communications across relevant jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with external immigration counsel and regional providers; for US matters, coordinate with Fragomen and ensure cases follow CoreWeave’s approved workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear playbooks for sponsorship, visa transfers, amendments, business travel, permanent residence, work authorization verification, and employment changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure immigration decisions and communications are consistent, timely, well documented, and appropriately escalated to Legal or executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong controls around start-date readiness, work location, right-to-work verification, and changes that may affect immigration status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Relocation and cross-border employment&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational framework for domestic and international relocations, including eligibility, approvals, vendor coordination, offer and relocation letters, payroll handoffs, and clawback administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Tax, Finance, Payroll, and People Business Partners on cross-border moves, entity considerations, permanent-establishment risk, compensation, benefits, and local compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop guidance for remote work across borders, temporary assignments, business visitors, transfers, and other mobile-worker scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the employee’s work location, effective date, immigration requirements, and relocation commitments are aligned before a move is finalized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Process, systems, and analytics&lt;/h3&gt;
