&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data Service Team serves as the experts on managing data infrastructures as services for CoreWeave. The data infra includes but is not limited to managed databases, data ingestion, data flow, and data lake and analysis for CoreWeave and its customers. This team is responsible for the development of use cases, discovery of innovative solutions, automation and operations of our data service infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a senior engineer manager with specialization in database space who can help us fulfill the goal of our data strategy and establish communication models for our data flow. This leadership role will work with a team of mixed skill engineers and have the opportunity to work on the full gamut of rewarding challenges that come with the business of building a cloud in a communicative, supportive, and high-performing environment. As a manager of the Data Service Team you will have the opportunity to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a world class engineering team by hiring and developing the best talent in the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have curiosity and hunger to solve very hard system level problems in order to run the world&#39;s most demanding and advanced AI workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement services to deliver data to teams with a focus on providing managed solutions through APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the performance, security, reliability, and scalability of our data services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish guidelines, guard rails for data access and storage for stakeholder teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with standards for data protection regulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze telemetry and system data to drive improvements in throughput, latency, and resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with platform, product, and infrastructure teams to deliver seamless storage capabilities across the stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow, change, invest in your teammates, be invested-in, share your ideas, listen to others, be curious, have fun, and, above all, be yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit? We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are some qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If a portion of this resonates with you, we’d love to talk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing or leading data service infra teams; 5+ years of hands-on software or infrastructure engineering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding one of the database internals: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Aurora, CockroachDB, TiDB, MongoDB, CosmosDB, Oracle, SQL Server, DB2, SAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on background with cloud native and separating compute from storage architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert on life of a query and life of a transaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy helping your colleagues achieve more with less effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience operating services in production and at scale and are versed in reliability engineering concepts such as the different types of testing, progressive deployments, error budgets, the role observability, and fault-tolerant design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand CAP theorem and concurrency models, can clearly define data models and establish guidelines around data management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited about new research in database systems.&lt;/li&gt;
