&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Special Projects Manager, to support our most challenging and high-priority initiatives across CoreWeave. You will join the Special Projects team, which operates as an internal consulting team and force-multiplier for the business, assembled to tackle our most challenging and high-priority initiatives. We take ownership of critical workstreams and support the CEO, CSO, CFO, CDO, GC, and other teams in cross-functional workstreams across CoreWeave. You will work with a variety of stakeholders across all levels of CoreWeave to support key executives and decision-makers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a generalist problem-solver, who can take ownership of a workstream, from problem statement through implementing and operating a solution. They will apply a consistent, rigorous toolkit of structured analysis, disciplined project management, and stakeholder influence to any business problem that they encounter.&amp;nbsp; Prior examples of Special Projects include our IPO, Board materials preparation, internal and external communications initiatives, new product development, M&amp;amp;A integrations, change management projects, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a consultative and strategic approach to developing and structuring problem statements, aggregating relevant research and data, conducting comprehensive analysis and assessments, providing actionable recommendations, implementing solutions, and measuring results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and present clear and concise communications for a variety of audiences, from the executive level to all company forums.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify key business challenges, scope opportunities for Special Projects support, and deliver solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently own end-to-end project management (PMO) for a portfolio of projects, orchestrating complex, cross-functional workstreams, proactively identifying risks, and meticulously overseeing implementation across all functional groups.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive decision-making through strategic reporting, insights, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are: &lt;/strong&gt;(This section has to be the technical and measurable requirement of the role, soft skills cannot be measured)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10 years of experience. A background in management consulting followed by in-house experience in corporate strategy, private equity, investment banking, product management, or a strategic chief of staff role is ideal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree is required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build trust and influence across all levels of an organization, fostering collaboration and accountability without ownership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to seamlessly shift between rolling up your sleeves to solve tactical problems with functional owners and advising C-level executives on high-level strategic planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to implement operational best practices, build scalable processes, and drive continuous improvement within an organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel and PowerPoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of cloud services, software businesses, digital infrastructure, or data centers is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit? &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
