&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Senior FW Technical Program Manager (TPM) to join our dynamic team focused on the New Product Introduction (NPI) of our next-generation GPU/CPU/Storage hardware. In this pivotal role, you will be instrumental in leading the cross-functional efforts from concept to mass production, ensuring the timely, high-quality, and cost-effective delivery of our innovative products that power the future of AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the complexities of hardware and firmware (BIOS/BMC/CPLD) development cycles, collaborate with world-class engineers, and influence strategic decisions to bring groundbreaking technology to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Technical Program Manager will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and drive the end-to-end NPI process for next-generation DC-SCM hardware and firmware, from initial concept and architecture definition through design, validation, manufacturing, and production ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and drive the process for FW development, qualification, and release process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop comprehensive program plans, roadmaps, and schedules, defining key milestones, dependencies, and critical paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Management, Hardware Design, Firmware, Software, Supply Chain, Manufacturing, Quality, and Operations teams to ensure alignment and seamless execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and identify potential risks, proactively develop mitigation strategies, and drive timely resolution of technical and logistical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and track program progress against established timelines, budget, and quality metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate regular cross-functional meetings, design reviews, and status updates, ensuring clear communication and accountability across all stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate program status, risks, and critical decisions to senior leadership and executive stakeholders with clarity and conciseness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of transparency, collaboration, and continuous improvement within the NPI process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage in technical discussions with engineering teams, challenge assumptions, and contribute to problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in technical program management within the hardware industry, with a strong focus on New Product Introduction (NPI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience delivering complex hardware and firmware products from concept to mass production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding and experience of firmware development lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical understanding of the FW components - BIOS/BMC/CPLD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead cross-functional teams, influence without direct authority, and drive consensus in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of GPU architectures, semiconductor fabrication processes, board design, power delivery, thermal management, and system-level integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in program management tools (e.g., Jira, Confluence, Sheet).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in Engineering or an MBA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GPU or other high-performance compute architecture NPI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with international manufacturing partners and supply chains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PDM/PLM systems and quality management processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with agile methodologies in a hardware development context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with industry standards and regulatory compliance for hardware products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp; We’re in an exciting stage of growth, scaling at an unprecedented speed. We are frequently challenging the norm, exploring new technologies and advancing the potential for hyperscale. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our products and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and provides the opportunity to develop innovative solutions to complex problems. As we continue to grow, opportunities within the organization are evolving and expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. If this resonates with you, come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
