&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Accountant, JV &amp;amp; VIE Accounting works across CoreWeave&#39;s joint ventures, investments and variable interest entities (VIEs). You will own the accounting for an assigned portfolio of JVs and investments, support the monthly close for VIE entities, coordinate with other accounting groups to ensure entries are recorded to the correct entities, and prepare and manage the workpapers that support financial statement disclosure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role well suited to someone who wants depth in consolidation, joint venture and structured entity accounting on a fast-moving program. You will prepare reconciliations and supporting workpapers for review, and work closely with teams across accounting, finance and legal. This role sits within the Leasing, Joint Venture, VIE and Construction Accounting team and reports to the Manager, JV &amp;amp; VIE Accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JV &amp;amp; VIE Entity Close&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the accounting for assigned JV entities and investments, including monthly close, financial statement preparation and partner reporting packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the monthly close for VIE entities, preparing journal entries and supporting schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the completeness and accuracy of activity recorded at each entity, ensuring transactions are coded to the correct entity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep open items documented and current, so that issues are resolved as activity lands rather than at period end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Transactions &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare distributions, capital calls and waterfall calculations for assigned JVs in accordance with the JV operating agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support communication with JV partners on reporting timelines, deliverables and accounting treatments for assigned entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Intercompany &amp;amp; Consolidation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare intercompany accounting across JV and VIE entities, including elimination entries and the reconciliation of intercompany balances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the consolidation of JV and VIE financial statements into CoreWeave&#39;s consolidated reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with other accounting groups to ensure entries are recorded to the correct entities, following cross-entity items through to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workpapers &amp;amp; Disclosure Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and manage the workpapers that support financial statement disclosure for joint ventures and VIEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document the basis for consolidation and disclosure conclusions, and keep supporting analyses current as entity structures change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reconciliation &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the period-end reconciliations for assigned entity accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate reconciling and outstanding items and follow them through to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare supporting schedules and variance explanations for review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls, Audit &amp;amp; Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain process documentation and evidence to meet Sarbanes-Oxley 404 requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits, including JV-level audits, maintaining audit readiness for assigned entities and responding to information requests on a timely basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process improvements, including automation opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of accounting experience, with exposure to consolidation, joint venture or structured entity accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience preparing journal entries, reconciliations and workpapers on a fixed close calendar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of US GAAP, including consolidation concepts; familiarity with operating in a SOX control environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel skills, including the ability to work accurately with large data sets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to coordinate across accounting groups and work cross-functionally with non-accounting teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ERP systems experience required; NetSuite an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain momentum in high-growth environments, including the capacity to act effectively when faced with ambiguity or incomplete data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational, time and self-management skills, and the ability to prioritize and work well under pressure to meet deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applicants must have work authorization that does not require sponsorship from the company now or in the future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong preference for candidates with joint venture, VIE (ASC 810) or equity method accounting experience, or a background supporting financial statement disclosure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Big 4 or public accounting experience; CPA or CPA candidate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with AI tools.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wondering if you&#39;re a good fit? We believe in investing in our people and value candidates who can bring their diverse experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are a few qualities we&#39;ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we&#39;d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You like being close to the detail — you&#39;d rather be the person who knows what every open item is than the one who asks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re curious about why an entry belongs where it does, not just where it was coded, and you follow the question until it makes sense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to build depth in joint venture and VIE accounting on a program where the volume and the pace will stretch you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We&#39;re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We&#39;re not afraid of a little chaos, and we&#39;re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities continue to expand. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $98,000&amp;nbsp; to $130,000 . The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
